# `fluid::heat`

Follows the temperature of the water through a run.

## Signature

```cpp
HeatResult heat(const Network &network, const Schedule &schedule, const Heat &thermal, const RouteOptions &route_options = {}, const Options &hydraulic_options = {});
```

## What It Does

A thermal specialisation of the route engine of `transport`: the same hydraulics, cells, mixing and tanks, with the exact heat exchange `T(t+Δt) = Ta + (T(t) - Ta) exp(-UA Δt / (ρ c_p V))` in every pipe and tank. Solved flow direction reverses both the boundary and the cell stencil.

## Parameters

`network`
: The compiled `Network`.

`schedule`
: The `Schedule`.

`thermal`
: The `Heat` record.

`route_options`
: The `RouteOptions`.

`hydraulic_options`
: The `Options` of the hydraulic solves.

## Returns

A `HeatResult`.

## Errors

Throws `std::invalid_argument` for invalid thermal or route options. Throws `std::runtime_error` for the failures of `run`.

## Interpretation and Use

Constant properties and one-way coupling are the contract: no pump heat, no temperature-dependent density or viscosity, no phase change. Solve the hydraulics at the temperature that matters.

